{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And thorns and thistles shall it grow for you.</b> The ground, when you sow it with kinds of seed, will grow thorns and thistles, cardoons and artichokes — and they are eaten by means of preparation (Beitzah 34)." "<b>And you shall eat the herb of the field.</b> And what curse is this? Was it not said to him in the blessing, ״הִנֵּה נָתַתִּי לָכֶם אֶת כָּל עֵשֶׂב זֹרֵעַ זֶרַע״ and so on? Rather, what is stated here at the head of the matter is ״cursed is the ground for your sake; in sorrow shall you eat of it״ — and after the sorrow, ״and thorns and thistles shall it grow for you״: when you sow it with legumes or garden vegetables, it will grow for you thorns and thistles and the rest of the herbs of the field, and you will eat them against your will."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:28.311860433Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}